      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a modern fintech context, arguments for \"equality of opportunity\" often center on the principle that the model should only use relevant, non-discriminatory information to assess merit. Proponents argue it ensures that everyone with similar underlying qualifications has a fair *chance* at approval, assuming the data is unbiased. However, critics rightfully point out that if the historical data reflects biased lending practices, optimizing for opportunity simply enshrines the \"chance\" within that already biased structure.",
